ssions that  are available  really teach you the mechanics of this  game and how you can really improve on  it right off the bat and  it's one of the key focuses of iron  harvest is  that i've had just as much fun playing  the single player aspect of the game as  i have  with skirmishing with my friends as well  which is a really unique aspect with rts  games because some rts games feel more  geared to the campaign while others feel  more geared towards the multiplayer  iron harvest is kind of like a perfect  blend of both  of those um playstyles  so you can have a blast with your  friends with this game as well as  you know play the campaign and really  enjoy the campaign i would recommend  uh when you're starting the game though  to definitely check out the campaign  first because there is a lot  to this game and how the cover mechanics  work so i want to talk a little bit  about the cover mechanics  so what really separates this game from  say your  age of empires or age of mythology or  any of those great classic rts games  those are my personal favorites  is of course the cover system and how uh  terrain plays a very important factor  in how you navigate and negotiate  your uh battles against other players or  the ai  so basically when you're using a cover  system you can order your troops to go  behind cover  and provides them a more defensive  position now  this can also lead to disadvantages as  well depending on what angle you're on  it leaves it requires you to be adaptive  and always be focusing on  what units you have different troops and  enemy types all come into play as well  in classic rts fashion  you know certain troops work against ba  against other troops better  uh for example you can't see it in in  this clip in particular but  standard infantry gets absolutely cut  down by  flamethrower troops but are also weak to  other varieties  of troops as well so it kind of gives  you that classic rts balance of  okay so my enemies playing these uh  characters so i need to play these  characters to counter them  but also the terrain and the environment  around you plays a huge factor into that  and one of the  coolest aspects of iron harvest i really  want to touch on  is the minimalist approach to building  and when i say a minimalist approach to  building i don't mean  necessarily that you can't build a lot  it's about  the options you have when you build so  basically when it comes to  making your troops and building up your  forces  you have two main uh production  facilities you can use your main  headquarters to produce your basic  engineers and your basic  foot infantry but you will need  basically a workshop that produces your  mechs  and a barracks that will produce your  troops everything else  is defensive based or defensive  orientated  or your base defense or cutting off key  choke  points or anything along those lines  from pill boxes to  mg nests to just simple sandbags to make  cover  uh for your troops and that's kind of  what makes this game really  special is the ability to craft the map  around what your game plan is there's a  perfect example of this  is when fighting cover to cover  sometimes if you have engineers in your  ranks you can build sandbag  fortifications if you want to hold the  point  because during multiplayer games of iron  harvest  you have to capture and hold points to  earn victory points  so the person with the most control  points obviously wins the game  or if you eliminate your opponent  however  what's really unique with iron harvest  is that you can build  defensive fortifications around these  control points so  say for example you take a bridge a  control point that's located near a  bridge you can build sandbags  uh up and mg nests around that  to better defend your control points you  can hold it longer  this is different than most rts games  where you would have to  simply use your soldiers to try to uh  to hold and choke the enemy off in  different areas  you have to use everything you have to  use the terrain you can use the  buildings you can hide and stash  uh troops and units inside uh  village houses and uh outlying buildings  um and this provides a certain element  of surprise that you can have on your  enemy as well as providing defensive  capabilities  it's just a really unique feature um and  what i really love is that  in the three different classes of iron  harvest you have your roost viets you  have your polanya  and you have your saxony all of these  different factions really provide you a  different uh play style polania is more  based around being middle it's very good  on defense it's very good on offense  but uh the roost fiats i've found in my  experience so far have been  astounding at offense meanwhile  saxony is very well geared to defense so  if you can take a point it's  really easy to hold it with saxony so  these factions really play  well around your play style and that's  what i think i most enjoy about this  game is it  took me very little time to find a  faction that really  spoke to me and really made me enjoy the  game this game's very  v has a very steep learning curve but  once you get a couple of games and it  starts feeling very natural and it's  very quick  and the games are intense and you you  you can lose hours in this game  very very quickly um because of how  immersive this game is  it's a wonderful game the soundtrack is  absolutely fantastic i can  not say enough about how great the  soundtrack is  uh from what i've heard so far in the  game um  and i'm just overall really impressed um  with the game as a cohesive whole from  what i've played in this open demo  because in the open demo in a very rare  form a very transparent  move and i want to give the developers  king art games a lot of credit for this  is that they did a rather brilliant move  this game has been basically an open  beta for the past few weeks  and in this open beta you are allowed to  access five campaign missions and  various skirmish maps and play  uh multiplayer games so you can pretty  get it you can get a pretty good idea of  what you want out of this game  and kind of one of the most brilliant  things about iron harvest  from what i've played so far has been  the fact that  it is really good at both of these  things  it is very balanced it is a lot of fun  it's great to play with my friends  especially if they're not good at rts  games because if you have a couple games  under your belt you can  really really take it to your friends  and it's just  overall a brilliant game and the  campaign is  very addictive um i finished the first  five campaign missions and left going  i want more and that's something very  rare that i find from an rts game  um because most of the time with rts  games the campaign feels  incredibly tacked on this is not the  case with iron harvest there is a very  interesting story that they've managed  to  lay out in front of you um with the  first five campaign missions i'm very  interested to see where the story leads  and there was mentions of a fourth  faction within the story  so i'm kind of interested to see what  that means uh going forward  post launch of course so it'll be very  interested to see  what more they do with this game it's  just overall it's a  brilliant game um and i really think  it's going to be a sleeper hit of  of the fall it releases september 1st  on pc steam there will be a console port  coming in 2021  it is currently as i've stated  previously it is available in open beta  on  steam you can search it on the steam  store at iron harvest  so i hope you have enjoyed this brief  preview  of iron harvest and i hope you've taken  away something from this or that you  will go check out this  uh very interesting and uh  mechanical game from king art  games um and we will have a full review  as well as guides on lords of gaming.net  in the coming week as the game goes past  review embargo  and releases on tuesday so we hope  to that you guys will tune into that  coverage as well  and we hope you guys have a blast with  what you have seen from  iron harvest so far and there is much  more to come  for in terms of content from us so i  appreciate you checking this out  once again i am nicholas downey the  assistant editor and  chief of lordsandgaming.net you can find  me  on twitter at undead 3xbi of course  don't forget to follow lordsofgaming.net  on twitter as well we will see you guys  next time
 

